<title>INDIA: Indian sugar prices fall on poor demand.</title>
<headline>Indian sugar prices fall on poor demand.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian sugar prices fell on Friday on low consumer demand and fresh retail interest, dealers said.</p>
<p>Ready delivery sugar s-30 fell by 10 rupees to 1,265/1,318 rupees per quintal while m-30 eased by the same margin to 1,300/1,360 rupees. Sugar mill delivery also lost gained ground by five rupees to 1,210/1,220 rupees.</p>
<p>-- Bombay Commodities +91-22-265 9000</p>
